   "kind": "imprecise_reference",
   "path": "handbook/parts/p15/probability-spaces-and-random-variables-w02c-p15-001.tex",
   "line_start": 117,
   "line_end": 126,
   "detail": "Case (d) of the owned notation convention identifies the counting-measure sum with \"the countable atomic formula of thm:p15-expectation-law-integral, taken with unit masses\"; that formula is stated for a probability space with masses p(omega), and counting measure on an infinite countable set is not a probability measure. The identification needs the nonnegative series theorem (thm:p15-nonnegative-integral-laws) rather than the expectation theorem."
